# UI patterns (AdminLTE namespace)

- **Template namespaces never cross-import CSS.** AdminLTE4 (Bootstrap 5, `src/assets/main-ltr.css` / `main-rtl.css`) owns `/apps/*` and auth pages. Never Tailwind classes in an AdminLTE view, never Bootstrap reliance inside a Tailwind island.
- **Loading states are mandatory.** Every data view renders skeleton → error-with-retry → empty/data through the shared primitives: `SkeletonBlock`, `ErrorState` (emits `retry`), `EmptyState`, `TableEmptyRow`, `useDetailLoader`. No view goes blank on fetch failure. `DataTable` extends the same order in its body and needs `:error` + `@retry`.
- **First load is explicit.** `useResource` never fetches on its own, and neither `useListingLiveUpdate` nor `useEchoResync` triggers the initial pull. A list view calls `useServerDataTable(fetchList, pagination)` (loads page 1) or `void fetchList()` in `onMounted`.
- **Navigation buttons are links.** A button whose only effect is `router.push` is a `<router-link :to>`, so hover reveals the URL. Real actions and `router.back()` stay `<button>`. A disabled nav uses `<router-link>` + `class="disabled"` + `aria-disabled="true"` + `tabindex="-1"`.
- **Row actions come from the server.** `RowActions.vue` renders the mapped `row.actions[]` from backend query-mode lists via `src/utils/mapQueryRowActions.ts` — never invent keys in the view, never add sibling buttons next to `RowActions`.
- **Swal only.** `src/lib/swal.ts` (`useAlert`, `confirmDialog`, `inputDialog`) — never native `alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`, never a `v-model` confirm component, never raw `Swal.fire` modals. `await showError(...)` before any `window.location.href` redirect. Never assign `document.body.className = ''` (Swal stores toast state on `<body>`).
- **Extract by concern.** Composable per concern (`src/composables/{domain}/use<Thing>.ts` — fetch, filters, selection, realtime, handlers) + section components (`src/components/{domain}/<Thing><Section|Card|Tab>.vue`, typed props/emits, `defineModel` for two-way). Realtime handlers live in the composable, never in an extracted section.
- **Heavy vendor widgets are async.** `FormSelect2` (jQuery + select2) is imported through `defineAsyncComponent(() => import(...))` so the vendor chunk loads only with its view.
- **Select2.** Grouping is one level deep — use `grouped` with explicit `children`, or `flattenTreeForSelect2()` for backend trees (`navigation/lookups/menus`). A programmatic `applyValue()` must not echo back through `update:modelValue` (an unhydrated ajax option would read as "cleared" and wipe stored pivots). Never "fix" an empty select by submitting it as empty: `MenuEditView` prunes only lookups that actually succeeded (`failedLookups` + `web.menus.hydrate_partial_warning`).
- **Dependent field visibility** is gated in four places, not one: the control (`v-if`), the option list (`computed`), a watcher that resets an invalid selection, and the request payload (null out the value). `disabled` (still visible) is different from hidden.
- **Safe URLs.** Internal redirects through `src/lib/safeRedirect.ts`; API-provided URLs, images, payment links, OTP links, and presigned PUT URLs through `src/utils/safeUrl.ts`.

